UPDATE generations SET description = 'Fresh text-only builds using E with corrected v2 part references, on-demand inspection and bounded mechanical feedback. No previous builds, images or visual feedback. Advisory original part targets. One scheduled run per model/brief; failures are retained separately. Not a controlled quality-improvement claim. OpenAI, 14 October: Luna/high, Sol 6.1/high and Astra/medium; published 17 of 18 (unpublished: gpt-6-astra destroyer, infrastructure-failure). Claude, 16-17 October, through the Claude CLI with tools off and a neutral system prompt: Haiku 5.5/high, Sonnet 5.5/high, Opus 5.5/high and Fable 5.1/medium; all 24 briefs published. 21 succeeded first time; at the owner''s request the three failures were retried: Opus Ewok succeeded on a fresh retry; Haiku temple succeeded with the unannounced 32,768 output-token cap raised to 128,000; Opus pelican succeeded when its session, which had asked for a fourth check, was told no checks remained and to return its final build. Gemini 3.8 Flash/high and Gemini 4 Argon/high were run through native agy on 17 October 2026: 9 accepted builds from 12 completed cases. Starting inputs are fresh and render-blind. The native-high profile uses a 128K host response guard because the CLI cannot set the earlier 32K server cap; the original Flash pilot keeps its 32K record. Transport recoveries remain in their own conversations, preserve source and assistance budgets, and are labelled in the archived runs. Failures remain archived.' WHERE id = 'e-reference-v2-20261014';
